{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8p38MAduX3o6NTqbTfd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J4nPErrFrefSkvCSEwNGtv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-09-leaving-player-resets-media-session; mkdir -p .nightralph; cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 09: leaving the player resets the media session\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/renderer/pages/player-page.js`: renamed the misnamed\n  `onComponentWillUnmount` to React's `componentWillUnmount`. It now\n  unloads every `audio,video` element (the main element and\n  `video#preview`): pause, removeAttribute('src'), load(). The old code\n  only handled the first match, and `src = ''` makes the element try to\n  load the page URL.\n- It also resets `navigator.mediaSession.metadata` to null and clears\n  the play/pause/nexttrack/previoustrack action handlers\n  (`MEDIA_SESSION_ACTIONS`). renderMedia() registers next and previous\n  only when the playlist has them, so a handler left over from the\n  last play would otherwise stick. Each setActionHandler call sits in\n  a try block because an engine may throw on an action it does not\n  support. The metadata reset no longer depends on a media tag being\n  found (the old code returned early before it).\n\n## Testing decision\n- No automated test was written. The spec's Testing Decisions list the\n  player page lifecycle as \"Not automated\" (pages are Vite-only and\n  cannot be required in the unit suite), and the ticket says it is\n  verified by hand. I chose not to add a source-scan test for the hook\n  name, because the spec rules out automating this.\n- `npm test` (lint + depcheck + build + 4224 unit tests) passes.\n\n## Manual checks (not run here, so they need a human with the app)\n- Play one file, close the player, play a different file: the system\n  media controls should show the second file's title.\n- After closing the player, the main and preview media elements no\n  longer hold a source.\nEOF\ncat >> src/renderer/pages/AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## React lifecycle hooks must use React's exact names\n\nA misnamed hook such as `onComponentWillUnmount` is just an unused\nmethod: React never calls it, and nothing warns you. Pages cannot be\nloaded in the unit suite, so check by hand that teardown code in a\npage actually runs. `player-page.js`'s `componentWillUnmount` unloads\nevery media element (main and `video#preview`) and resets\n`navigator.mediaSession`. `renderMedia()` sets the metadata only while\nit is `null`, so that reset is what lets the next play show fresh\nmetadata.\nEOF\ngit add src/renderer/pages && git commit -qm \"Leaving the player unloads its media and resets the media session\n\nThe unmount hook was named onComponentWillUnmount, so React never\ncalled it. Rename it to componentWillUnmount, unload both the main and\npreview media elements, and reset the media session metadata and\naction handlers so the next play sets fresh ones.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":51542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13e2c60c-45b8-4fbe-9566-585462c93ca3","uuid":"22a8053f-454f-4ee6-9cda-fc1df027bc90","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:11:02.344Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8p386JEcTaCQkCexgt9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01J4nPErrFrefSkvCSEwNGtv":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-09-leaving-player-resets-media-session; mkdir -p .nightralph; cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 09: leaving the player resets the media session\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/renderer/pages/player-page.js`: renamed the misnamed\n  `onComponentWillUnmount` to React's `componentWillUnmount`. It now\n  unloads every `audio,video` element (the main element and\n  `video#preview`): pause, removeAttribute('src'), load(). The old code\n  only handled the first match, and `src = ''` makes the element try to\n  load the page URL.\n- It also resets `navigator.mediaSession.metadata` to null and clears\n  the play/pause/nexttrack/previoustrack action handlers\n  (`MEDIA_SESSION_ACTIONS`). renderMedia() registers next and previous\n  only when the playlist has them, so a handler left over from the\n  last play would otherwise stick. Each setActionHandler call sits in\n  a try block because an engine may throw on an action it does not\n  support. The metadata reset no longer depends on a media tag being\n  found (the old code returned early before it).\n\n## Testing decision\n- No automated test was written. The spec's Testing Decisions list the\n  player page lifecycle as \"Not automated\" (pages are Vite-only and\n  cannot be required in the unit suite), and the ticket says it is\n  verified by hand. I chose not to add a source-scan test for the hook\n  name, because the spec rules out automating this.\n- `npm test` (lint + depcheck + build + 4224 unit tests) passes.\n\n## Manual checks (not run here, so they need a human with the app)\n- Play one file, close the player, play a different file: the system\n  media controls should show the second file's title.\n- After closing the player, the main and preview media elements no\n  longer hold a source.\nEOF\ncat >> src/renderer/pages/AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## React lifecycle hooks must use React's exact names\n\nA misnamed hook such as `onComponentWillUnmount` is just an unused\nmethod: React never calls it, and nothing warns you. Pages cannot be\nloaded in the unit suite, so check by hand that teardown code in a\npage actually runs. `player-page.js`'s `componentWillUnmount` unloads\nevery media element (main and `video#preview`) and resets\n`navigator.mediaSession`. `renderMedia()` sets the metadata only while\nit is `null`, so that reset is what lets the next play show fresh\nmetadata.\nEOF\ngit add src/renderer/pages && git commit -qm \"Leaving the player unloads its media and resets the media session\n\nThe unmount hook was named onComponentWillUnmount, so React never\ncalled it. Rename it to componentWillUnmount, unload both the main and\npreview media elements, and reset the media session metadata and\naction handlers so the next play sets fresh ones.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short"}}}
